@* this component has a generic type. when called in Painting form, it is DateOnly *@
@typeparam TValue

@code {
  // set default! to tell compiler "we will set this via the framework as it takes in the parameter"
  [Parameter, EditorRequired]
  public string Label { get; set; } = default!;

  // The current value of the input
  [Parameter]
  public TValue? Value { get; set; }

  // onChange callback
  [Parameter]
  public EventCallback<TValue?> ValueChanged { get; set; }

  // Func<TValue?> would be a compiled function -- you could call it and get a
  // value, nothing more. Expression<Func<TValue?>> is the *code itself* kept as
  // inspectable data: a little tree saying "read the property DatePainted off
  // this object". Blazor reads that tree to learn which model property this
  // input is bound to, which is how a validation error finds the right field,
  // and how the name="Input.DatePainted" attribute gets generated for the POST.
  //
  // The caller never writes this. @bind-Value="Input.DatePainted" expands into
  // all three parameters at once, and the compiler supplies "() => Input.DatePainted"
  // here automatically.
  [Parameter]
  public Expression<Func<TValue?>> ValueExpression { get; set; } = default!;
  private string ElementId => FieldIdentifier.Create(ValueExpression).FieldName;
}

<div>
  @* InputDate is a framework component that renders <input type="date"> and
     handles parsing text into a DateOnly. TValue="TValue" hands our type
     parameter through to it.

     q: how does it know it can accept TValue, what if that isn't a date type?
     shouldn't it be TValue extends Date or something?

     We forward all three binding parameters rather than re-binding. Forwarding
     ValueExpression is the important one: if we wrote @bind-Value="Value" here,
     the inner input would think it was bound to *our* Value property, and both
     the validation matching and the form's name attribute would point at the
     wrong thing. 

q: clearly there is some concept of "Binding" that I need to understand first
     *@
  <FieldLayout Label="@Label" ValueExpression="ValueExpression" Context="elementId">
    <InputDate class="artist-shop-field-input" id="@elementId" Value="Value" ValueChanged="ValueChanged"
               ValueExpression="ValueExpression" />
  </FieldLayout>
</div>
